er","confidence":0.85,"rationale":"Grocery stores, restaurants, and other food retailers that purchase and operate commercial refrigeration equipment would be affected by whether they must buy equipment meeting the new standards."},{"industry":"hospitality","confidence":0.75,"rationale":"Hotels and restaurants use commercial refrigeration equipment and would be affected by the regulatory requirements for equipment they purchase."},{"industry":"utilities-electric","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"Electric utilities would see different demand patterns depending on whether commercial refrigeration equipment must meet higher efficiency standards."}],"plainSummary":"This joint resolution would cancel a Department of Energy rule that set stricter energy efficiency standards for commercial refrigerators, freezers, and similar equipment used by businesses. The rule, published in January 2025, would have required this equipment to meet new energy conservation standards by January 2029. If this resolution passes, those updated standards would be eliminated and the equipment would not need to comply with the new requirements.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"Anyone who buys food.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"N000189","score":0.0257116644139778},"overlapCount":14},"meaning":{"percentile":19.77570683936187,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[],"unattributedShare":0.8165217424396809}},{"billId":"119-hjres-24","bioguideId":"P000605","cycle":2026,"score":0.0027980313672593196,"matches":[{"industry":"hospitality","donorAmount":20972.03,"donorShare":0.007557940511871203,"billConfidence":0.7,"contribution":0.0017346092978065056},{"industry":"retail-consumer","donorAmount":10000,"donorShare":0.0036038192353678705,"billConfidence":0.9,"contribution":0.0010634220694528142}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence